  "label": "User projected onto the visual material of the father holding his newborn daughter",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man (father) holding and kissing his newborn daughter, as the image and text together create an intimate, universal moment of paternal love. The absence of explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you' means the projection is implicit, inviting the user to identify with the emotional experience or the universal theme of fatherhood depicted. The user is not explicitly addressed, but the scene's tenderness and the text's descriptive nature encourage identification with the father-daughter bond.",
